# npth -- New Portable Threads library, GnuPG's thread abstraction
#
# Part of the six-recipe GnuPG chain that flatpak's hard dependency on gpgme
# makes unavoidable: gpgme does not implement crypto, it spawns the gpg binary
# and talks to it over libassuan, so packaging gpgme means packaging gnupg and
# everything beneath it. Flathub's repository signatures are GPG.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://gnupg.org/ftp/gcrypt/npth/npth-1.8.tar.bz2
SRC_SHA256=8bd24b4f23a3065d6e5b26e98aba9ce783ea4fd781069c1b35d149694e90ca3e
SRC_DIR=npth-1.8

# --disable-static RESTATES A DEFAULT HERE AND IS KEPT ANYWAY, which is worth
# saying plainly rather than letting it look load-bearing. configure reports
# "--enable-static[=PKGS] build static libraries [default=no]", so libtool
# already builds shared only. It is passed because every other library recipe in
# this tree passes it, and because the default belongs to libtool rather than to
# this package -- a future libtool or a future upstream could flip it without
# anything here noticing. Consistency plus a pinned outcome, not a fix.
#
# --disable-tests. THE TESTS ARE ON BY DEFAULT: configure offers --disable-tests,
# which is the spelling used when a feature is enabled unless switched off. Build
# time only -- nothing is installed either way -- but it is named so the absence
# is a decision.
#
# NOT PASSED: --enable-install-npth-config. Off by default, and the same
# deprecated-config-script shape as libgpg-error's gpg-error-config: consumers
# use pkg-config. Recorded because the reflex on a later configure failure is to
# switch these on, and it is the wrong lever.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --disable-tests"
